<http://data.silknow.org/actor/618fa4a6-a54f-300e-b552-9e81a5d5b1bc>
        a                         ecrm:E39_Actor ;
        rdfs:label                "Charles Mather Ffoulke is said to have purchased both tapestries from an unidentified dealer in Munich (unpublished letters.) The dealer did not specify the source, but stated that the tapestries came from a \"royal house.\" Collection Charles Mather Ffoulke, Washington, D.C. Collection French and Company, New York. Collection George Robert White, Boston. Collection Mrs. Harriet J. Bradbury, Boston. Bequest of Mrs. Harriet J. Bradbury, July 3. / Bequest of Mrs. Harriet J. Bradbury" ;
        ecrm:P1_is_identified_by  "Charles Mather Ffoulke is said to have purchased both tapestries from an unidentified dealer in Munich (unpublished letters.) The dealer did not specify the source, but stated that the tapestries came from a \"royal house.\" Collection Charles Mather Ffoulke, Washington, D.C. Collection French and Company, New York. Collection George Robert White, Boston. Collection Mrs. Harriet J. Bradbury, Boston. Bequest of Mrs. Harriet J. Bradbury, July 3. / Bequest of Mrs. Harriet J. Bradbury" .

